  "result": "Perfect! All 244 tests pass. I've successfully added credit notes functionality:\n\n## What was added:\n\n**src/errors.js** \u2014 Added `CREDIT_TOO_HIGH` error:\n- Returns when credit note amount exceeds invoice total\n\n**src/credits.js** \u2014 New module with two functions:\n\n- `nextCreditNoteNumber(existingNumbers, issueDate)` \u2014 Generates credit note numbers:\n  - Format: CN-YYYY-NNNN (separate counter from invoices)\n  - Maintains independent numbering per year\n  - Ignores invoice (INV) numbers in existingNumbers\n\n- `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` \u2014 Creates credit notes:\n  - Works on issued, partially_paid, or paid invoices only\n  - Returns `NOT_ISSUED` for draft invoices\n  - Returns `AMOUNT_INVALID` for zero, negative, or non-integer amounts\n  - Returns `CREDIT_TOO_HIGH` if amount exceeds invoice total\n  - Returns `ok(creditNote)` with: `{ number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date }`\n  - Uses credit note's issue date (not invoice date) for year in numbering\n\n**test/credits.test.js** \u2014 29 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Credit note numbering (format, year handling, gaps, malformed numbers)\n- Credit note creation for all applicable invoice statuses\n- Amount validation (zero, negative, non-integer, exceeds total)\n- Edge cases (equal to total, very large/small amounts)\n- Multiple credit notes per invoice\n- Mixed invoice and credit note number handling\n- Voucher integration in total calculations\n- Customer ID and reason preservation\n\nAll 244 tests pass with no regressions.",
